{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Gingham"}],"title":"Appearance"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The table follows the system look by default: system fonts and colors,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alternating row backgrounds, a rounded selection like the Finder sidebar,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overlay scrollers, light and dark mode, the user’s accent color, and a Liquid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Glass summary bar on macOS 26 (a header material on earlier systems). Rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scroll underneath the summary bar.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Sizes","level":3,"text":"Sizes","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Property"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Default"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowHeight","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"24"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rows’ height, unless the delegate gives rows their own ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableViewRowHeights","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") or a column wraps text (then the height of a row of one line)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/headerRowHeight","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"28"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The column titles."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/groupHeaderHeight","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"24"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The group band, only shown when there are groups."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryRowHeight","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"30"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The summary row."}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"anchor":"Fonts-colors-and-density","level":3,"text":"Fonts, colors and density","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The table uses the system fonts and colors, following light and dark mode,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accent color and contrast settings. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/tableStyle"},{"text":" changes them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where an app needs its own look; anything left ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stays the system’s:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["table.tableStyle = GHTableStyle(","    fontSize: 15,                      \/\/ cells and the summary row","    headerFontSize: 12,                \/\/ column titles","    textColor: .labelColor,","    backgroundColor: NSColor(named: \"TableBackground\"),","    stripeColors: [.clear, NSColor(named: \"Stripe\")!],","    groupRowColor: NSColor(named: \"GroupRow\"))","table.density = .compact               \/\/ or .regular (24 points), .spacious"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/density"},{"text":" sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowHeight"},{"text":" for the style’s font,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a little, some or more room around the text, like Finder’s list sizes;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it follows a later font size change. Give the style the same color objects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each time (the renderer resolves each color once per appearance).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Rows-and-selection","level":3,"text":"Rows and selection","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/usesAlternatingRowBackgroundColors","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" stripes the rows with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s alternating content colors."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/showsVerticalGridLines","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" draws thin lines between columns."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/selectionHighlightStyle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".rounded"},{"type":"text","text":" (inset, rounded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corners, like macOS lists; the table then keeps a small margin at its edges)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fullWidth"},{"type":"text","text":" (a plain band across the whole row, like classic tables)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The selection is shown in the accent color while the table is focused and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in gray otherwise."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Highlighting-rows-by-their-data","level":3,"text":"Highlighting rows by their data","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The delegate can tint a row’s background and put a colored marker at its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leading edge, for example green for profitable campaigns and red for losing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ones:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Created once: the table asks for every visible row while scrolling.","static let profitTint = NSColor.systemGreen.withAlphaComponent(0.10)","static let lossTint = NSColor.systemRed.withAlphaComponent(0.10)","","func tableView(_ tableView: GHTableView, backgroundColorForRow row: Int) -> NSColor? {","    let roi = data.campaigns[row].roi","    return roi > 0 ? Self.profitTint : roi < 0 ? Self.lossTint : nil","}","","func tableView(_ tableView: GHTableView, markerColorForRow row: Int) -> NSColor? {","    data.campaigns[row].isOverBudget ? .systemOrange : nil","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use light, translucent tints so text stays readable, and return the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"color objects every time (static constants): the table compares them to skip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unchanged rows."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tints replace the alternating stripes of their rows. Selected rows show the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selection instead of the tint, and keep the marker."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"System colors like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"systemGreen"},{"type":"text","text":" adapt to dark mode and accent changes by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table asks when rows come into view and on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/reloadData()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". If the condition behind a tint changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without a data change, call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reloadData()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Empty-state","level":3,"text":"Empty state","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"While there are no rows, the table shows ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/emptyStateText"},{"text":", or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your own ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/emptyStateView"},{"text":" (for example with a button to create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the first record). The table places it; the app says what it is.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without any data (the data source has no rows), the table shows only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty state, centered: no header, row stripes or summary row."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowFilter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" hides every row, the columns stay and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty state shows in the rows area. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/FilteringAndSearch","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While the data updates (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/isUpdatingData","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), the spinner"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes its place, and it comes back if there are still no rows. There’s no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"need to clear the text while loading."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Scrolling","level":3,"text":"Scrolling","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The table scrolls by itself, like a scroll view:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"trackpads scroll with momentum and bounce at the top and bottom; turn the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bounce off with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/bouncesVertically","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gestures lock to the axis they start on, so vertical scrolling doesn’t drift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sideways;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"overlay scrollers appear while scrolling and expand under the pointer;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with “Show scroll bars: Always” in System Settings, the table shows classic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scrollers that take up space;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"clicking the scroller track pages, and holding it keeps paging;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"scrolling on an axis the table has nothing to scroll on goes to the view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that contains it, like a nested scroll view’s: a table of a few rows in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form scrolls the form (alone in a window, its rows still bounce)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In code, read ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset"},{"text":" and scroll with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/scroll(to:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/scrollRowToVisible(_:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didScrollNotification"},{"text":" tells every change of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset"},{"text":" once the rows are laid out there, where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"NSTableView apps watch the clip view’s bounds: for example, load the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"page when ","type":"text"},{"code":"rowIndexes(in: table.bounds)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reaches the last rows.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/willStartLiveScrollNotification"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didLiveScrollNotification"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didEndLiveScrollNotification"},{"text":" follow the user’s scrolling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"like a scroll view’s: a trackpad gesture or a drag of the overlay scroller,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ending with its momentum. Never make","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the table the document of an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSScrollView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a form around it in one is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fine).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Localization","level":3,"text":"Localization","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The table’s own texts — its menus (the summary scope, columns, grouping,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"views), the column filter and save view dialogs, Undo names and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"VoiceOver reads — are localized in English and Russian; the summary scope","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"titles can be replaced with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryScopeTitles"},{"text":". Everything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"else the user reads — column","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"titles, tool tips, menus, empty state texts, tags and mark labels — comes from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your app, localized as you like. Numbers and dates are formatted in the user’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"locale.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Right-to-left-languages","level":3,"text":"Right-to-left languages","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In a right-to-left interface (Arabic, Hebrew; the table follows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/userInterfaceLayoutDirection"},{"text":", which AppKit sets from the app’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language) the whole table is mirrored, like AppKit’s own controls:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first column is at the right; leading frozen columns stay at the right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge and trailing ones at the left; the vertical scroller is at the left."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each cell’s content is mirrored within it: leading text at the right,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numbers aligned to the trailing side (the left), tags listed from the right,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data bars growing from the right, outline and group indents and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disclosure triangles at the right, the triangles of collapsed rows pointing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left. Text itself reads as written: every line moves whole, so Arabic,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Hebrew and mixed text keep their order."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Column titles put the filter button and the sort arrow at their left;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"columns resize from their left edge and move by dragging the other way."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Left Arrow goes to the next column and Right Arrow back (on group headers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and tree rows, Right Arrow collapses and Left Arrow expands); Tab still goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the next column. Swiping a row to the right shows its trailing actions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the left."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" still counts from the leading end: 0 shows the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first columns, at the right. Printing and PDF put the first column at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right too."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set ","type":"text"},{"code":"userInterfaceLayoutDirection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" yourself to show one table mirrored or not,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the app’s language.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/Appearance"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gingham\/appearance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Appearance and Behavior","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/KeyboardAndAccessibility","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHSelectionHighlightStyle","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableStyle","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableDensity"],"anchor":"Appearance-and-Behavior","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"Adjust sizes, highlight rows by their data, and choose how selection and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scrolling look.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableStyle":{"url":"\/d